cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the article below and this repository."
title: "MEGAN_SC: a reproducible MEGANv3.21 biogenic-emissions pipeline for Santa Catarina, Brazil, 2003-2025"
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of the MEGANv3.21 emission code with a Google Earth Engine data layer, used to build a monthly
  0.025-degree inventory of biogenic VOCs, soil NO and CO for Santa Catarina, Brazil (2003-2025). The repository holds
  the engine and its input and run procedures (src/megan_sc/fixes.py), a stage-by-stage comparison with the official
  Fortran executables, the notebooks of the production run, its automatic checks, the TROPOMI formaldehyde evaluation,
  the sensitivity tests, the model output (as release archives), a one-command reproduction of every number, table
  and figure of this example (reproduce.py), and notebooks that run the same pipeline for any region and period.
type: software
authors:
